PURPOSE of /kernel/microcode/sanity
Description: Microcode Sanity Check
Author: Rachel Sibley <rasibley@redhat.com>

Description:
The purpose of this script is not to verify the update worked, but to
verify no regressions are found during the update, such as failures in
the logs, system failing to boot, reinstalling the pkgs, microcode
service failures, etc. Verifying the microcode was updated on the system
will continue to be done manually with each new release as it is difficult
to automate which system requires the update.  RHEL7, the AMD microcode
has been moved to the linux-firmware package. This script will be wrapped
around the /distribution/utils/power-cycle task and kick off with every
new brew build.
